For me, things really started turning around when I got familiar with
the joy of missile weapons.   Get yourself a stack of daggers and kill
your enemies from far away. It's amazing how much less of a problem
mind flayers, nymphs et al cause when they can't touch you.

I can't really give you more specific advice without more info on your
games.  General suggestions for the mines:

1)  Have a light source or other way of seeing things at a distance. As
I've said before,  the Light Shop is a guaranteed shop for a reason :).


2) Search the ground very, very carefully. The place is stiff with
traps.

3) Just thought of this one: There are a fair number of cats and dogs
in the mines. Save your tripe from Sokoban and make lots of pets. Let
them wander the level and find all the traps. Better them than you :).


4) Stay out of melee if you can.  Most creatures can't kill what they
can't touch.

5) Engrave "E" to get a safe spot.

6) Have an escape scroll or wand handy so you can get out of trouble.

7) Practice.  It takes a lot of death to get good at this game.  Stick
with it, and the drought will end.

Just general suggestions.  Wish you the best.

